## Evidence (what the gate reads — skills/testing/test-results-sidecar.md)

```bash
P="agent_state/phases/{{PHASE}}"; mkdir -p "$P/junit" "$P/reports"
git add tests/integration && git commit -m "phase {{PHASE}}: integration tests (TC-…)"   # commit first
CMD="$(jq -r '.commands["test:integration"]' agent_state/config/verify-commands.json)"
[ -n "$CMD" ] && [ "$CMD" != null ] || { echo "BLOCKED: no test:integration command in verify-commands.json"; exit 1; }
PHASE={{PHASE}} bash -c "$CMD" > "$P/junit/integration.log" 2>&1; RC=$?
python3 .claude/hooks/junit-to-sidecar.py --tier integration --command "$CMD" --exit-code $RC \
  --priorities "$P/tc_priorities.json" --out "$P/reports/integration_tests.json" "$P/junit/integration.xml"
```

- No retries to green. Flaky = failing. Quarantine only with an issue link and an expiry of at most
  14 days, in the sidecar's `quarantined[]`.
- Go: `-count=1` (no cached results), and `-race` where cgo allows.
- `test_runner` re-runs the tier in Wave 3v and refreshes `integration_tests.json` from its own run.

